course: dictionary
lesson: 109
title: Administrative words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Administrative means about organising and running a school, business or government: the paperwork, planning and office work that keeps things working. «The school hired three new administrative staff to answer calls and sort the forms.» Staff who answer calls and sort forms are office workers, so administrative must mean about running the school.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try "office-work staff" in place of "administrative staff" and it still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: Geography uses the word too. An administrative area is a part of a country with its own local government. The word also appears in official phrases such as «administrative segregation», which is the US official name for keeping a prisoner alone in a cell as a punishment.
fact: Administrative means about organising and running a school, business or government.
fact: «Administrative staff» means office workers who keep things running smoothly.
fact: «Administrative tasks» are jobs like filing forms, planning and sending letters.
fact: An administrative area is a part of a country with its own local government.
fact: «Administrative segregation» is the US official phrase for solitary confinement, keeping a prisoner alone in a cell as a punishment.
exercise: «The school hired three new administrative staff to answer calls and sort the forms.» What does administrative mean here? | About playing sport | About painting pictures | About cooking lunch | *About running the school, like office work
exercise: Which of these is an administrative task? | Singing in a choir | Painting a mural | Climbing a tree | *Filing forms and booking rooms
exercise: «The council runs the administrative area of the town.» Find and copy the word that means about running things. | council | *administrative | town | the
exercise: Which phrase means money spent on paperwork and running an office? | Luminous costs | Ancient costs | *Administrative costs | Glum costs
test: «The administrative area of the county has its own local government.» What is an administrative area? | A kind of shop | A type of cloud | A sports team | *A part of a country with its own local government
test: Which phrase means office workers who keep a school running? | Barely staff | Famished staff | Treacherous staff | *Administrative staff
exam: Which best explains «administrative» in «the administrative tasks of the business»? | Light that glows | *The paperwork and organising that keeps a business running | Very old tools | Dangerous work up a steep hill
